<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quit India Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1942</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as August Movement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Quit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Movement was a mass campaign launched by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a> on 8 August 1942, demanding an immediate end to British rule. The British arrested <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a> and the Congress leadership at once, and the protests, strikes and sabotage that followed were suppressed with great force. It was the last great mass campaign of the independence movement before 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quit-india-movement.jpg" alt="Quit India Movement" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Quit_india_Movement_Collage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
